WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.357
Lady Kou ran into the courthouse early the next morning.

2
00:00:06.358 --> 00:00:12.821
With tears in her eyes, she told the judge that she had lied the day before.

3
00:00:12.822 --> 00:00:16.179
"The Tang Monk and his companions are innocent."

4
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.151
[g@Lady Kou sniffed.

5
00:00:18.152 --> 00:00:20.608
"Please release them."@g]

6
00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:22.373
[g@The judge nodded.

7
00:00:22.374 --> 00:00:25.567
"I was going to release the prisoners this morning."@g]

8
00:00:25.568 --> 00:00:30.487
He explained how the Wandering Spirit had visited him the night before.

9
00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:32.497
Lady Kou gasped.

10
00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.172
[g@"My husband visited me last night!

11
00:00:35.173 --> 00:00:39.012
We must release the prisoners at once."@g]

12
00:00:39.013 --> 00:00:43.961
[g@They hurried to the Tang Monk's cell.

13
00:00:43.962 --> 00:00:52.432
A guard swung open the cell door.@g]

14
00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:58.626
"I'm glad to be out of there," said Wujing.

15
00:00:58.627 --> 00:01:02.096
[g@"Me too," said Bajie with a yawn.

16
00:01:02.097 --> 00:01:05.372
"The beds were very uncomfortable."@g]

17
00:01:05.373 --> 00:01:08.348
Lady Kou bowed to the Tang Monk.

18
00:01:08.349 --> 00:01:12.210
"I framed you for killing my husband," she said.

19
00:01:12.211 --> 00:01:13.829
[g@"Please forgive me.

20
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.765
It was a terrible thing to do."@g]

21
00:01:16.766 --> 00:01:19.828
[g@"That's right!" shouted Wukong.

22
00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:23.395
"It was a really terrible thing to do!"@g]

23
00:01:23.396 --> 00:01:27.187
[g@The Tang Monk put his hand on the monkey's shoulder.

24
00:01:27.188 --> 00:01:28.946
"Don't yell, Wukong."@g]

25
00:01:28.947 --> 00:01:31.114
[g@He looked at Lady Kou.

26
00:01:31.115 --> 00:01:32.584
"We forgive you.@g]

27
00:01:32.585 --> 00:01:34.890
[g@The squire was a kind man.

28
00:01:34.891 --> 00:01:39.811
His death is a terrible tragedy."@g]

29
00:01:39.812 --> 00:01:41.849
[g@Wukong rubbed his chin.

30
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:45.544
"I can probably bring him back to life."@g]

31
00:01:45.545 --> 00:01:48.799
Lady Kou and the judge were shocked.

32
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.602
"Can you really do that?" asked Lady Kou.

33
00:01:52.603 --> 00:01:54.444
[g@The Tang Monk smiled.

34
00:01:54.445 --> 00:01:56.135
"Yes, he can.@g]

35
00:01:56.136 --> 00:02:00.192
Wukong brought the king of the Black Rooster Kingdom back to life."

36
00:02:00.193 --> 00:02:02.103
He turned to the monkey.

37
00:02:02.104 --> 00:02:04.785
[g@"The sage Laozi helped you that time.

38
00:02:04.786 --> 00:02:06.972
Will you ask him for help again?"@g]

39
00:02:06.973 --> 00:02:09.179
[g@"No," said Wukong.

40
00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.684
"Laozi doesn't really like me.@g]

41
00:02:11.685 --> 00:02:19.341
I'll go to the Land of Darkness and talk to the Judge of the Dead instead."

42
00:02:19.342 --> 00:02:24.912
When Wukong entered the Palace of Darkness, the Judge of the Dead frowned.

43
00:02:24.913 --> 00:02:27.801
"Why are you here, Wukong?

44
00:02:27.802 --> 00:02:34.935
You already made yourself immortal by crossing out your name in the Directory."

45
00:02:34.936 --> 00:02:37.405
Wukong laughed.

46
00:02:37.406 --> 00:02:40.408
[g@"I wondered if you would remember that.

47
00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:43.097
I'm looking for Squire Kou's name."@g]

48
00:02:43.098 --> 00:02:50.132
"Squire Kou?" The judge opened the Directory and flipped through some pages.

49
00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:55.459
"Ah, yes. He died two days ago.

50
00:02:55.460 --> 00:03:00.407
He now works for the bodhisattva Dayuan in the Jade Palace.

51
00:03:00.408 --> 00:03:04.926
It's here in the Land of Darkness."

52
00:03:04.927 --> 00:03:08.879
Wukong went to the Jade Palace.

53
00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:13.060
"Greetings, Sun Wukong," said the bodhisattva.

54
00:03:13.061 --> 00:03:16.791
"Greetings, Bodhisattva." The monkey bowed.

55
00:03:16.792 --> 00:03:22.363
"Two nights ago a friend of mine, Squire Kou, was killed and brought here.

56
00:03:22.364 --> 00:03:25.436
I would like to bring him back to Earth."

57
00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:28.001
[g@The bodhisattva raised an eyebrow.

58
00:03:28.002 --> 00:03:30.569
"You want him to return to life?"@g]

59
00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.862
"Yes," said Wukong.

60
00:03:32.863 --> 00:03:37.964
"I'm helping the Tang Monk reach the Western Paradise to fetch the True Scriptures.

61
00:03:37.965 --> 00:03:41.143
The squire was very kind to us."

62
00:03:41.144 --> 00:03:43.022
The bodhisattva smiled.

63
00:03:43.023 --> 00:03:50.152
"Very well. The squire may return to Earth until it's time for him to come back here."

64
00:03:50.153 --> 00:03:57.451
The bodhisattva brought Wukong to an office.

65
00:03:57.452 --> 00:04:05.788
Squire Kou was sitting behind a large desk, smiling, as he studied some documents.

66
00:04:05.789 --> 00:04:09.473
His eyes sparkled when he saw Wukong.

67
00:04:09.474 --> 00:04:12.886
[g@"It's good to see you, Wukong!" said the squire.

68
00:04:12.887 --> 00:04:14.804
"What are you doing here?"@g]

69
00:04:14.805 --> 00:04:18.161
"I have good news," said the monkey.

70
00:04:18.162 --> 00:04:20.484
[g@"Your life isn't over yet.

71
00:04:20.485 --> 00:04:22.881
I'm taking you back to Earth."@g]

72
00:04:22.882 --> 00:04:25.227
[g@The squire looked confused.

73
00:04:25.228 --> 00:04:29.291
He glanced at the bodhisattva.@g]

74
00:04:29.292 --> 00:04:31.374
[g@The bodhisattva nodded.

75
00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:33.577
"You may return to Earth.@g]

76
00:04:33.578 --> 00:04:38.055
When your life is over, you will return to your job here."

77
00:04:38.056 --> 00:04:41.675
The squire came out from behind his desk and bowed.

78
00:04:41.676 --> 00:04:44.097
"Thank you, Bodhisattva.

79
00:04:44.098 --> 00:04:48.617
I am happy here, but I would love to see my wife and friends again."

80
00:04:48.618 --> 00:04:51.630
[g@Wukong moved closer to the squire.

81
00:04:51.631 --> 00:04:54.223
"You'll be home soon, Squire."@g]

82
00:04:54.224 --> 00:05:04.318
The monkey recited a spell, and the squire vanished.

